# rekeys -- a q: that was reworded, and the template that replaced it. a card
# is keyed by its q: template, so a rewording files its review history under
# a key no block answers to; cards_rehome (lib/cards) reads this to carry the
# row to the new wording. level-id, old template, new template, tab-separated.
# a row only ever moves a card that would otherwise be orphaned, so an entry
# can stay here for good.
